      *================================================================*
      * ACCTPOST - APPLY A DAY OF MOVEMENTS TO THE ACCOUNT MASTER      *
      *                                                                *
      * THE BALANCED-LINE MATCH-MERGE.  ONE SEQUENTIAL PASS OVER TWO   *
      * SORTED FILES, PRODUCING A NEW MASTER AND A REJECTS FILE.       *
      *                                                                *
      * THE MASTER IS NOT READ INTO MEMORY AND NEVER WILL BE.  MATCH-  *
      * MERGE EXISTS BECAUSE THE MASTER DOES NOT FIT.  A VERSION THAT  *
      * LOADS IT INTO A TABLE WOULD PASS EVERY TEST IN THIS PACKAGE AND*
      * DESTROY ITS ENTIRE PURPOSE.                                    *
      *                                                                *
      * INPUT   ACCTMAST.DAT  ACCTREC, 100 BYTES, ASCENDING BY ACCT-REF*
      *         MOVEMENT.DAT  MOVEREC, 120 BYTES, ASCENDING BY MOV-    *
      * ACCT-REF                                                       *
      * OUTPUT  ACCTNEW.DAT   ACCTREC, THE NEW MASTER                  *
      *         REJECTS.DAT   REJREC, 200 BYTES                        *
      *                                                                *
      * REJECTION IS A BUSINESS OUTCOME, NOT AN ABEND.  A MOVEMENT THAT*
      * CANNOT BE APPLIED IS WRITTEN TO THE REJECTS FILE AND THE RUN   *
      * CONTINUES.  CONTROL TOTALS MUST BALANCE: READ = APPLIED +      *
      * REJECTED.                                                      *
      *                                                                *
      * COMPILE:                                                       *
      *   cobc -x -std=ibm -Wall -I mainframe/copybook ACCTPOST.CBL    *
      *================================================================*
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. ACCTPOST.
       AUTHOR. TESSERA BANK CORE BANKING.

       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.

      *    ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL, NEVER LINE SEQUENTIAL.  A
      *    COMP-3 AMOUNT CAN CONTAIN X'0A' OR X'0D'.  LINE
      *    SEQUENTIAL WOULD CORRUPT EVERY PACKED FIELD AND WOULD
      *    LOOK AS THOUGH IT HAD WORKED.

           SELECT ACCT-MASTER-IN  ASSIGN TO 'ACCTMAST.DAT'
               ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
               ACCESS MODE IS SEQUENTIAL
               FILE STATUS IS WS-MASTER-STATUS.

           SELECT MOVEMENT-IN     ASSIGN TO 'MOVEMENT.DAT'
               ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
               ACCESS MODE IS SEQUENTIAL
               FILE STATUS IS WS-MOVE-STATUS.

           SELECT ACCT-MASTER-OUT ASSIGN TO 'ACCTNEW.DAT'
               ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
               ACCESS MODE IS SEQUENTIAL
               FILE STATUS IS WS-NEWMAST-STATUS.

           SELECT REJECT-OUT      ASSIGN TO 'REJECTS.DAT'
               ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
               ACCESS MODE IS SEQUENTIAL
               FILE STATUS IS WS-REJECT-STATUS.

       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.

      *    THE FD RECORDS ARE UNSTRUCTURED AND EVERY READ IS 'INTO'
      *    WORKING STORAGE.  THAT WAY EACH COPYBOOK IS INCLUDED EXACTLY
      *    ONCE IN THE PROGRAM, AND THE HELD MASTER RECORD SURVIVES THE
      *    NEXT READ - WHICH THE MATCH-MERGE DEPENDS ON.

       FD  ACCT-MASTER-IN
           RECORD CONTAINS 100 CHARACTERS.
       01  MASTER-IN-RECORD        PIC X(100).

       FD  MOVEMENT-IN
           RECORD CONTAINS 120 CHARACTERS.
       01  MOVEMENT-IN-RECORD      PIC X(120).

       FD  ACCT-MASTER-OUT
           RECORD CONTAINS 100 CHARACTERS.
       01  NEW-ACCOUNT-RECORD      PIC X(100).

       FD  REJECT-OUT
           RECORD CONTAINS 200 CHARACTERS.
       01  REJECT-OUT-RECORD       PIC X(200).

       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.

       COPY ACCTREC.

       COPY MOVEREC.

       COPY REJREC.

       01  WS-FILE-STATUS.
           05  WS-MASTER-STATUS      PIC X(02) VALUE SPACES.
           05  WS-MOVE-STATUS        PIC X(02) VALUE SPACES.
           05  WS-NEWMAST-STATUS     PIC X(02) VALUE SPACES.
           05  WS-REJECT-STATUS      PIC X(02) VALUE SPACES.

       01  WS-FLAGS.
           05  WS-MASTER-EOF         PIC X(01) VALUE 'N'.
               88  MASTER-EOF                  VALUE 'Y'.
           05  WS-MOVE-EOF           PIC X(01) VALUE 'N'.
               88  MOVE-EOF                    VALUE 'Y'.

      *    THE BALANCED LINE.  AT EACH STEP THE LOWER OF THE TWO
      *    KEYS IS TAKEN; HIGH-VALUES STANDS IN FOR A FILE THAT HAS
      *    REACHED END, SO IT SORTS LAST AND THE OTHER FILE DRAINS.
       01  WS-CURRENT-KEY            PIC X(16) VALUE SPACES.
       01  WS-MASTER-KEY             PIC X(16) VALUE SPACES.
       01  WS-MOVE-KEY               PIC X(16) VALUE SPACES.
       01  WS-MASTER-HELD            PIC X(01) VALUE 'N'.
           88  MASTER-HELD                     VALUE 'Y'.

      *    THE SIGNED EFFECT OF ONE MOVEMENT ON THE HELD ACCOUNT.
      *    POSITIVE INCREASES THE BALANCE, NEGATIVE REDUCES IT; WHICH
      *    IS WHICH DEPENDS ON THE ACCOUNT TYPE, NOT ON THE DIRECTION
      *    ALONE.  SEE THE NORMAL-BALANCE TABLE IN THE CANONICAL MODEL.
      *    THE SAME SCALE AS THE MONEY THEY HOLD.  AN INTERMEDIATE
      *    WITHOUT V99 SILENTLY TRUNCATES EVERY AMOUNT TO WHOLE UNITS,
      *    WHICH IS HOW A REJECTION THAT SHOULD FIRE QUIETLY DOES NOT.
       01  WS-EFFECT             PIC S9(13)V99 COMP-3 VALUE ZERO.
       01  WS-NEW-BOOKED         PIC S9(13)V99 COMP-3 VALUE ZERO.

      *    REJECTION REASONS.  DEFINED HERE BECAUSE THE CANONICAL DATA
      *    MODEL DELEGATES THEM TO THIS PROGRAM.  REJECTION IS A
      *    BUSINESS OUTCOME, NOT AN ABEND: THE MOVEMENT IS WRITTEN TO
      *    THE REJECTS FILE AND THE RUN CARRIES ON.
       01  WS-REASON-CODE            PIC X(04) VALUE SPACES.
       01  WS-REASON-TEXT            PIC X(40) VALUE SPACES.
       01  WS-RUN-TIMESTAMP          PIC X(14) VALUE SPACES.
       01  WS-CURRENT-DATE-DATA.
           05  WS-CD-DATE            PIC 9(08).
           05  WS-CD-TIME            PIC 9(06).
           05  FILLER                PIC X(07).

       01  WS-TOTALS.
           05  WS-MOVE-READ          PIC 9(09) COMP-3 VALUE ZERO.
           05  WS-MOVE-APPLIED       PIC 9(09) COMP-3 VALUE ZERO.
           05  WS-MOVE-REJECTED      PIC 9(09) COMP-3 VALUE ZERO.
           05  WS-MASTER-READ        PIC 9(09) COMP-3 VALUE ZERO.
           05  WS-MASTER-WRITTEN     PIC 9(09) COMP-3 VALUE ZERO.
           05  WS-VALUE-MOVED    PIC S9(13)V99 COMP-3 VALUE ZERO.

       01  WS-EDIT.
           05  WS-COUNT-ED           PIC ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZ9.
           05  WS-VALUE-ED           PIC -Z(13)9.99.

       01  WS-RETURN-CODE            PIC 9(02) VALUE ZERO.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.

       MAIN-PARA.
           PERFORM SET-RUN-TIMESTAMP
           PERFORM OPEN-FILES
           PERFORM PRIME-READS
           PERFORM MATCH-MERGE
           PERFORM WRITE-CONTROL-TOTALS
           PERFORM CLOSE-FILES
           MOVE WS-RETURN-CODE TO RETURN-CODE
           STOP RUN.

      *    THE RUN TIMESTAMP COMES FROM THE JOB, NOT THE WALL CLOCK,
      *    WHEN ONE IS SUPPLIED.  A BATCH JOB TAKES ITS BUSINESS DATE
      *    FROM JCL, AND IT MAKES THE REJECTS FILE REPRODUCIBLE SO THE
      *    HARNESS CAN COMPARE IT BYTE FOR BYTE.
       SET-RUN-TIMESTAMP.
           ACCEPT WS-RUN-TIMESTAMP FROM ENVIRONMENT 'ACCTPOST_RUN_TS'
           IF WS-RUN-TIMESTAMP = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES
               MOVE FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE TO WS-CURRENT-DATE-DATA
               STRING WS-CD-DATE WS-CD-TIME
                   DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-RUN-TIMESTAMP
           END-IF.

       OPEN-FILES.
           OPEN INPUT  ACCT-MASTER-IN
           OPEN INPUT  MOVEMENT-IN
           OPEN OUTPUT ACCT-MASTER-OUT
           OPEN OUTPUT REJECT-OUT
           IF WS-MASTER-STATUS NOT = '00'
               DISPLAY 'ACCTPOST ABEND OPEN ACCTMAST ' WS-MASTER-STATUS
               MOVE 12 TO WS-RETURN-CODE
               PERFORM CLOSE-FILES
               MOVE WS-RETURN-CODE TO RETURN-CODE
               STOP RUN
           END-IF
           IF WS-MOVE-STATUS NOT = '00'
               DISPLAY 'ACCTPOST ABEND OPEN MOVEMENT ' WS-MOVE-STATUS
               MOVE 12 TO WS-RETURN-CODE
               PERFORM CLOSE-FILES
               MOVE WS-RETURN-CODE TO RETURN-CODE
               STOP RUN
           END-IF.

       CLOSE-FILES.
           CLOSE ACCT-MASTER-IN
           CLOSE MOVEMENT-IN
           CLOSE ACCT-MASTER-OUT
           CLOSE REJECT-OUT.

       PRIME-READS.
           PERFORM READ-MASTER
           PERFORM READ-MOVEMENT.

       READ-MASTER.
           READ ACCT-MASTER-IN INTO ACCOUNT-RECORD
               AT END
                   SET MASTER-EOF TO TRUE
                   MOVE HIGH-VALUES TO WS-MASTER-KEY
               NOT AT END
                   ADD 1 TO WS-MASTER-READ
                   MOVE ACCT-REF TO WS-MASTER-KEY
           END-READ.

       READ-MOVEMENT.
           READ MOVEMENT-IN INTO MOVEMENT-RECORD
               AT END
                   SET MOVE-EOF TO TRUE
                   MOVE HIGH-VALUES TO WS-MOVE-KEY
               NOT AT END
                   ADD 1 TO WS-MOVE-READ
                   MOVE MOV-ACCT-REF TO WS-MOVE-KEY
           END-READ.

      *    THE PASS ITSELF.  TAKE THE LOWER KEY, HOLD THE MASTER
      *    RECORD IF IT MATCHES, DRAIN EVERY MOVEMENT FOR THAT KEY,
      *    THEN WRITE THE MASTER RECORD ONCE.
       MATCH-MERGE.
           PERFORM UNTIL MASTER-EOF AND MOVE-EOF
               IF WS-MASTER-KEY <= WS-MOVE-KEY
                   MOVE WS-MASTER-KEY TO WS-CURRENT-KEY
               ELSE
                   MOVE WS-MOVE-KEY TO WS-CURRENT-KEY
               END-IF

               MOVE 'N' TO WS-MASTER-HELD
               IF WS-MASTER-KEY = WS-CURRENT-KEY AND NOT MASTER-EOF
                   SET MASTER-HELD TO TRUE
               END-IF

      *        THE MASTER RECORD STAYS IN ACCOUNT-RECORD FOR THE WHOLE
      *        OF ITS KEY.  MOVEMENTS MUTATE IT IN PLACE, IT IS WRITTEN
      *        ONCE, AND ONLY THEN IS THE NEXT ONE READ.  READING AHEAD
      *        INTO THE SAME AREA WOULD OVERWRITE THE RECORD STILL BEING
      *        WORKED ON - WHICH IT DID, ON THE FIRST ATTEMPT.
               PERFORM APPLY-MOVEMENTS-FOR-KEY
                   UNTIL WS-MOVE-KEY NOT = WS-CURRENT-KEY

               IF MASTER-HELD
                   WRITE NEW-ACCOUNT-RECORD FROM ACCOUNT-RECORD
                   ADD 1 TO WS-MASTER-WRITTEN
                   PERFORM READ-MASTER
               END-IF
           END-PERFORM.

       APPLY-MOVEMENTS-FOR-KEY.
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-REASON-CODE
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-REASON-TEXT

           IF NOT MASTER-HELD
      *        A MOVEMENT NEVER CREATES AN ACCOUNT.
               MOVE 'R001' TO WS-REASON-CODE
               MOVE 'ACCOUNT NOT FOUND IN MASTER' TO WS-REASON-TEXT
           ELSE
               PERFORM VALIDATE-MOVEMENT
           END-IF

           IF WS-REASON-CODE = SPACES
               PERFORM APPLY-ONE-MOVEMENT
           ELSE
               PERFORM WRITE-REJECT
           END-IF

           PERFORM READ-MOVEMENT.

      *    ORDER MATTERS.  THE MOVEMENT'S OWN VALIDITY IS CHECKED FIRST,
      *    THEN THE ACCOUNT, THEN THE PAIRING, THEN THE BALANCE.  IF THE
      *    CURRENCY MISMATCH CHECK CAME FIRST, R004 WOULD BE
      *    UNREACHABLE FOR EVERY ACCOUNT NOT ALREADY IN THAT CURRENCY -
      *    AND R004 IS THE MORE FUNDAMENTAL PROBLEM.
       VALIDATE-MOVEMENT.
           IF MOV-AMOUNT NOT > ZERO
               MOVE 'R006' TO WS-REASON-CODE
               MOVE 'AMOUNT NOT POSITIVE' TO WS-REASON-TEXT
           ELSE
               PERFORM VALIDATE-CURRENCY-SCALE
           END-IF.

      *    STRATUM 0 CARRIES SCALE-2 CURRENCIES ONLY.  PIC S9(13)V99
      *    HARD-CODES TWO DECIMALS, SO A JPY AMOUNT WOULD BE MISSTATED A
      *    HUNDREDFOLD.  THE INTEGRATION TIER REJECTS THESE BEFORE THEY
      *    ARRIVE; THIS CORE DOES NOT TRUST ITS FEEDS AND CHECKS AGAIN.
       VALIDATE-CURRENCY-SCALE.
           IF MOV-CURRENCY = 'PLN' OR MOV-CURRENCY = 'EUR'
               OR MOV-CURRENCY = 'USD' OR MOV-CURRENCY = 'GBP'
               OR MOV-CURRENCY = 'CHF'
               PERFORM VALIDATE-ACCOUNT-STATUS
           ELSE
               MOVE 'R004' TO WS-REASON-CODE
               MOVE 'CURRENCY SCALE NOT SUPPORTED' TO WS-REASON-TEXT
           END-IF.

       VALIDATE-ACCOUNT-STATUS.
           IF ACCT-STATUS = 'OPEN'
               PERFORM VALIDATE-CURRENCY-MATCH
           ELSE
               MOVE 'R002' TO WS-REASON-CODE
               MOVE 'ACCOUNT NOT OPEN' TO WS-REASON-TEXT
           END-IF.

       VALIDATE-CURRENCY-MATCH.
           IF MOV-CURRENCY = ACCT-CURRENCY
               PERFORM VALIDATE-BALANCE
           ELSE
               MOVE 'R003' TO WS-REASON-CODE
               MOVE 'CURRENCY DIFFERS FROM ACCOUNT' TO WS-REASON-TEXT
           END-IF.

      *    THIS CORE HAS NO ARRANGED-OVERDRAFT CONCEPT - THE MASTER
      *    CARRIES NO LIMIT FIELD - SO A CUSTOMER ACCOUNT MAY NOT BE
      *    TAKEN BELOW ZERO AT ALL.  CREDITS ARE NEVER REFUSED ON
      *    BALANCE GROUNDS: AN ACCOUNT CAN ALREADY BE NEGATIVE FROM
      *    LEGACY STATE, AND REFUSING A REPAYMENT WOULD BE ABSURD.
       VALIDATE-BALANCE.
           PERFORM COMPUTE-EFFECT
           COMPUTE WS-NEW-BOOKED = ACCT-BOOKED-BAL + WS-EFFECT
           IF WS-EFFECT < ZERO AND WS-NEW-BOOKED < ZERO
               AND ACCT-TYPE = 'LIABILITY'
               MOVE 'R005' TO WS-REASON-CODE
               MOVE 'DEBIT EXCEEDS AVAILABLE BALANCE'
                   TO WS-REASON-TEXT
           END-IF.

      *    THE MOVEMENT IS CARRIED VERBATIM IN THE FIRST 120 BYTES, SO A
      *    REJECT CAN BE RE-PRESENTED TO A LATER RUN WITHOUT BEING
      *    RE-ENCODED.
       WRITE-REJECT.
           MOVE MOVEMENT-RECORD TO REJ-MOVEMENT
           MOVE WS-REASON-CODE TO REJ-REASON-CODE
           MOVE WS-REASON-TEXT TO REJ-REASON-TEXT
           MOVE WS-RUN-TIMESTAMP TO REJ-DETECTED-TS
           WRITE REJECT-OUT-RECORD FROM REJECT-RECORD
           ADD 1 TO WS-MOVE-REJECTED.

      *    THE SIGNED EFFECT.  AN ASSET OR EXPENSE ACCOUNT INCREASES ON
      *    THE DEBIT SIDE; EVERYTHING ELSE INCREASES ON THE CREDIT SIDE.
      *    A CUSTOMER CURRENT ACCOUNT IS A LIABILITY OF THE BANK, SO A
      *    CREDIT TO IT INCREASES WHAT THE BANK OWES.
       COMPUTE-EFFECT.
           IF ACCT-TYPE = 'ASSET' OR ACCT-TYPE = 'EXPENSE'
               IF MOV-DIRECTION = 'D'
                   MOVE MOV-AMOUNT TO WS-EFFECT
               ELSE
                   COMPUTE WS-EFFECT = 0 - MOV-AMOUNT
               END-IF
           ELSE
               IF MOV-DIRECTION = 'C'
                   MOVE MOV-AMOUNT TO WS-EFFECT
               ELSE
                   COMPUTE WS-EFFECT = 0 - MOV-AMOUNT
               END-IF
           END-IF.

       APPLY-ONE-MOVEMENT.
           PERFORM COMPUTE-EFFECT
           ADD WS-EFFECT TO ACCT-BOOKED-BAL
           ADD WS-EFFECT TO ACCT-AVAIL-BAL
           MOVE MOV-VALUE-DATE TO ACCT-LAST-MOVE-DATE
           ADD MOV-AMOUNT TO WS-VALUE-MOVED
           ADD 1 TO WS-MOVE-APPLIED.

       WRITE-CONTROL-TOTALS.
           MOVE WS-MASTER-READ TO WS-COUNT-ED
           DISPLAY 'ACCTPOST CTL MASTER-READ    ' WS-COUNT-ED
           MOVE WS-MASTER-WRITTEN TO WS-COUNT-ED
           DISPLAY 'ACCTPOST CTL MASTER-WRITTEN ' WS-COUNT-ED
           MOVE WS-MOVE-READ TO WS-COUNT-ED
           DISPLAY 'ACCTPOST CTL MOVE-READ      ' WS-COUNT-ED
           MOVE WS-MOVE-APPLIED TO WS-COUNT-ED
           DISPLAY 'ACCTPOST CTL MOVE-APPLIED   ' WS-COUNT-ED
           MOVE WS-MOVE-REJECTED TO WS-COUNT-ED
           DISPLAY 'ACCTPOST CTL MOVE-REJECTED  ' WS-COUNT-ED
           MOVE WS-VALUE-MOVED TO WS-VALUE-ED
           DISPLAY 'ACCTPOST CTL VALUE-MOVED    ' WS-VALUE-ED

           IF WS-MOVE-READ NOT = WS-MOVE-APPLIED + WS-MOVE-REJECTED
               DISPLAY 'ACCTPOST CTL OUT-OF-BALANCE'
               MOVE 12 TO WS-RETURN-CODE
           ELSE
               DISPLAY 'ACCTPOST CTL BALANCED'
           END-IF.
